  "interpretation": "Original fixed low windows are lower-arrival windows, not qualified low states. User/system costs divide aggregate counters by phase completions, not per-job CPU. Edge accounting compares all pre-offer and post-arrival CPU with the excess over N times busy-window aggregate CPU/completion; it is a conditional reference calculation, not identification of a mechanism or attribution to individual jobs. Clock/counter bounds are not statistical confidence intervals. No state criteria, windows, thresholds or original reports were changed."
